# Fill in after deploying, then restart `npm run dev`.
VITE_FACTORY_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
VITE_FACTORY_V2_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
VITE_LOCKER_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
# CensusCurve — the bonding-curve trading venue (buy/sell + graduation). Required for live trading.
VITE_CURVE_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Current Robinhood Chain TESTNET deployment (2026-09-17, PF-style curve + 3-second launch tax; chainId 46630).
# Copy these four into .env together with the testnet block below. Mainnet addresses come from deploy.js at cutover.
# VITE_FACTORY_ADDRESS=0xf4509155753697d667B5954Ed93A65CE509C10f6
# VITE_FACTORY_V2_ADDRESS=0x0B3cd6f5c203caF0F7415E2A65897542c22872d2
# VITE_LOCKER_ADDRESS=0x50D1793aC84090Ddd871d576eaf5ea7663cFD6A7
# VITE_CURVE_ADDRESS=0xedc8e7286dC3D7C785dCED080d8366ABDbA65e40
# VITE_WETH=0x823F4ef19CCE787C7D10483896eE0102F48A88eb
# VITE_SWAP_ROUTER=0x0F134877161c8C3Ab9A87e9B4c0e0280BF0D1D82
# VITE_V3_FACTORY=0x1e572f531c74f16B760e308DA684895B94A9D8E1

# Chain selection. Leave unset for Robinhood mainnet (4663). For any NON-mainnet build (e.g. testnet
# 46630) the Uniswap addresses below are REQUIRED, not optional: off mainnet they no longer fall back to
# mainnet addresses (that silent bleed is fixed — CX-H3), so an unset VITE_WETH/VITE_SWAP_ROUTER becomes
# the zero address and trading fails loudly. Use the values from uniswap.robinhoodTestnet.json.
# VITE_CHAIN_ID=46630
# VITE_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com
# VITE_WETH=0x823F4ef19CCE787C7D10483896eE0102F48A88eb          # WETH9 (testnet)
# VITE_SWAP_ROUTER=0x0F134877161c8C3Ab9A87e9B4c0e0280BF0D1D82   # SwapRouter02 (testnet)
# VITE_V3_FACTORY=0x1e572f531c74f16B760e308DA684895B94A9D8E1    # required for graduated-pool pricing off mainnet

# --- Impact-aware trade quoting (CX-H1) ---
# Uniswap V3 QuoterV2 for the graduated-pool trade path: without it the "you receive ~" and the on-chain
# minimum-out fall back to an impact-free spot estimate (covered only by the user's slippage), which
# reverts normal trades on a shallow pool. Verify the Robinhood Chain QuoterV2 address on-chain, then set:
# VITE_QUOTER=0x...           # Robinhood Chain QuoterV2 (mainnet; verify before setting)

# --- Board data source / scan cost (CX-S2) ---
# Without an indexer the board scans factory logs from VITE_FROM_BLOCK. Leave it 0 for a fresh chain,
# but on mainnet set it to the factory DEPLOY block so the scan doesn't walk all of chain history.
# VITE_FROM_BLOCK=0
# When the Census indexer is deployed, point the board at it (fast, scales) instead of scanning:
# VITE_INDEXER_URL=https://indexer.census.example

# --- 0x best-price trading (src/lib/zeroex.ts via the api/zeroex.ts serverless proxy) ---
# The 0x API key is SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Set ZEROX_API_KEY (NO VITE_ prefix) in the Vercel project env so
# it never gets inlined into the browser bundle. Optional: ZEROX_API_BASE (defaults to https://api.0x.org).
# The client hits the proxy at /api/zeroex; override with VITE_ZEROX_PROXY only if you host it elsewhere.
# VITE_ZEROX_PROXY=/api/zeroex
# Local dev: `vite` alone won't run the serverless function — use `vercel dev` (with ZEROX_API_KEY set) to
# exercise live 0x quotes locally. Without it, the live quote stays blank and trades fall back to the pool.

# --- Privy: "Sign up" (email / Google / Apple / X + an embedded wallet on Robinhood Chain) next to "Connect wallet" ---
# Unset = wallet-only connect (the Privy SDK is never downloaded). App ID and Client ID are PUBLIC identifiers
# from the Privy dashboard. The Privy App Secret must NEVER go in a VITE_ variable (it would ship to browsers).
# VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=cmtvxr5kv01g90cib2d6q5tjk   # the "Census Fund" Privy app (public ID; exactly 25 chars)
# VITE_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=               # optional app client for this environment (e.g. one allowing localhost)
# VITE_PRIVY_LOGIN_METHODS=email     # must match the dashboard; add google,apple,twitter once those are switched on there
